---
import '../styles/showcase.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Services | Websites, software & automation | Wear Valley Digital" description="Websites, bespoke software and automation shaped around your business. Explore practical services, the delivery process and ongoing Care from Wear Valley Digital." canonical="https://wearvalleydigital.com/services/">
  <section class="showcase-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Digital services / Founder-led delivery</p>
      <h1>Build around your business</h1>
      <p class="lede">A new website, a tool for your team or a better way to connect your systems. Start with what your customers and colleagues need, then work directly with Andy Clarke to shape, build and test the solution.</p>
      <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/enquire/">Discuss your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#websites">Explore the services ↓</a></div>
      <div class="hero-foot"><span>Local in-person work in Weardale</span><span>Remote delivery across the UK</span><span>Scope and quote agreed before the build</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <article class="card" id="websites">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Your digital presence</p>
        <h2>Websites</h2>
        <p>Give people a clear picture of your business and a useful next step, whether that is an enquiry, a visit or a link to your existing booking service.</p>
        <p>For example: a local business explaining its services and area, or a community organisation bringing its information and contact details together.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Content structure and design that reflect your brand.</li>
          <li>Layouts for phones and larger screens, with accessible navigation.</li>
          <li>Clear service information, search foundations and contact routes.</li>
          <li>An agreed hosting, publishing and handover arrangement.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/enquire/">Discuss a website →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="software">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Your specialist workflow</p>
        <h2>Bespoke software</h2>
        <p>Build an application around a specific business need, with the people using it involved in shaping how it works.</p>
        <p>For example: track customer requests, organise records, manage an internal process or give a team a shared view of its work.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Workflows and screens shaped around your requirements.</li>
          <li>Appropriate access for the people using the application.</li>
          <li>Agreed integrations, data handling and export needs.</li>
          <li>Testing of the important journeys, followed by handover guidance.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/enquire/">Discuss an application →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="automation">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Your time, better spent</p>
        <h2>Automation &amp; integrations</h2>
        <p>Reduce repeated manual steps and connect the systems you already use, where those systems support the connection.</p>
        <p>For example: turn an enquiry into a customer record, prepare a recurring report or notify the right person when a task needs attention.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A review of the current process and its repetitive steps.</li>
          <li>Clear rules for what starts the workflow and what it changes.</li>
          <li>Checks, exception handling and human review where needed.</li>
          <li>Testing with agreed examples and guidance for operating it.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/enquire/">Discuss an automation →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work together</p>
      <h2>From first conversation to handover</h2>
      <p>You bring the business knowledge; I bring engineering, testing and automation experience. The exact deliverables are agreed for your project.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Discovery.</strong> Understand the problem, who the work is for, what you already have and any budget or timing constraints.</li>
        <li><strong>Scope and quote.</strong> Agree what will be delivered, what you need to provide, how we will check it and the proposed delivery plan. Hosting, third-party costs and ongoing support are discussed here.</li>
        <li><strong>Build and review.</strong> Develop the agreed solution and give you opportunities to review the work. If a new requirement emerges, we discuss its effect on scope, cost and timing.</li>
        <li><strong>Test and refine.</strong> Check the important tasks and customer journeys, relevant screen sizes and agreed integrations. Resolve issues against the agreed scope before handover.</li>
        <li><strong>Launch and handover.</strong> Prepare the agreed release, provide the access and guidance you need, and confirm how hosting, maintenance and future changes will be handled.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/enquire/">Tell us about your project →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="service-band">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Keeping your project working</p>
      <h2>Care after launch</h2>
      <p>Care covers the agreed maintenance, security updates, monitoring, backup and recovery arrangements, and fault investigation. The scope, support arrangements and costs are set out in your quote.</p>
      <p>Care is required with WVD-managed hosting and optional with customer-managed hosting. New features, redesigns and routine content changes are scoped separately, so you can decide what to develop next.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/insights/care-and-development/">Read the Care and development guide →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the studio</p>
      <h2>Our own products, in development</h2>
      <p>WVD is also developing Human V1, PECP, Salon and Wedding, with Hospitality in planning. Their project pages show the ideas, prototypes and current development stages.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/products/">Explore the work in development →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="service-cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="showcase-callout">
        <div><h2>What would you like to improve?</h2><p>Tell us about your business, the problem you want to solve and any timing constraints. You can prepare a project enquiry or email hello@wearvalleydigital.com directly.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@wearvalleydigital.com">Email an enquiry</a></div></div>
        <a class="button" href="/enquire/">Start your project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
